1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,810
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,640
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:08,110
(Episode 33)

5
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:43,850
So Yeon.

6
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,090
Gosh, yes. I'll be right out.

7
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:01,830
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

8
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,840
This is new. You don't usually
get off work this early.

9
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:07,240
Why do you think?

10
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:08,940
I get it.

11
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:10,480
You want to have dinner with me
for a change.

12
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:15,410
I was actually going to be
really upset if we went...

13
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,780
another week without a date.

14
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:19,380
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

15
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:21,020
Do you really not know
what today is?

16
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:23,560
What day is it?

17
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:25,920
Never mind.

18
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,890
Come on, what day is it?

19
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:31,030
How do you forget every year?

20
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:33,060
Did you really not know
today was my dad's memorial service?

21
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,070
Oh, right.

22
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:38,570
If I were you, I would at least
write it down somewhere.

23
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,610
I'm sorry.
I'll buy the fruit on the way.

24
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:45,740
Let's go.

25
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:52,480
Let me see.

26
00:01:57,590 --> 00:01:58,590
How is it?

27
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,860
You are really good
at cooking, So Yeon.

28
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:06,400
I'm good at making
everything my husband liked.

29
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,330
Right, a memorial service
is nothing special.

30
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,700
You just prepare the food he liked
when he was alive.

31
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:13,400
Your husband's spirit
will enjoy the meal.

32
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:16,980
Really?
Should I add more sesame seeds?

33
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,910
Sesame seeds.

34
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,820
If I had known
it was your father's memorial,

35
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,080
I would've dressed up a bit more.

36
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:26,180
Should we buy some clothes
on the way?

37
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,190
Don't bother.

38
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,900
Let's hurry.

39
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,500
Ms. Park must be having a hard time
working all alone.

40
00:02:58,050 --> 00:02:59,050
Mom.

41
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,390
Mr. Seok Jin, you're home.

42
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,090
Did you make
a lot of delicious food?

43
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:04,160
Yes.

44
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:08,490
- I see you came too.
- Of course.

45
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,060
It's Father's memorial,
so of course I came.

46
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:16,300
Something smells good.

47
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,740
Ms. Park, what should I do first?

48
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,840
There's no need for you
to do anything.

49
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,240
You don't have to help.

50
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:24,580
I'll help you out a bit.

51
00:03:34,490 --> 00:03:36,450
The table layout looks
a bit unusual.

52
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,490
Seok Jin said
it's like a birthday party.

53
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:45,000
Those were
all my husband's favorite foods.

54
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,000
How can a memorial meal
be a birthday meal?

55
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,260
What's this?

56
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,130
Was it Dad's?

57
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,750
I prepared your usual drink.

58
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:44,660
Thank you, Director Joo.

59
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:48,030
Around this time every year,
you have trouble sleeping.

60
00:04:50,090 --> 00:04:51,230
Do I?

61
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:54,430
You usually take sleeping pills
around this time every year,

62
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:58,170
but I thought a glass of whiskey
would be less harmful than pills.

63
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:02,070
I suppose so.

64
00:05:03,610 --> 00:05:06,540
Anyway, you're very attentive,
Director Joo.

65
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,110
You even notice
all of those little things.

66
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:11,650
Of course.

67
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,290
I have spent so many years
by your side,

68
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,990
so I should naturally know.

69
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:20,060
You say it comes naturally to you,

70
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,360
but why can't my wife see it?

71
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,030
Well then, get some rest.

72
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:46,620
Are you having fun, Seok Jin?

73
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:48,290
Yes.

74
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,460
Is that an airplane?

75
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,660
You won't be too late today, right?

76
00:06:00,330 --> 00:06:03,030
Seok Jin has been looking forward
to this play so much.

77
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,900
I'll check out the factory today
and head straight home.

78
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,170
Are you sure? You promised.

79
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:11,980
Get ready with Seok Jin
and wait for me.

80
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,780
- I'll be home early.
- Okay.

81
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:15,410
Have a good day, honey.

82
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:27,020
Mom, when is Dad coming home?

83
00:06:28,230 --> 00:06:31,100
He said he'll be here soon.
Let's wait just a little longer.

84
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:36,170
Hello.

85
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:37,370
Is this Cha Seong Woo's residence?

86
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,340
That's right. How can I help you?

87
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:41,470
You need to come
to the hospital right away.

88
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,280
Your husband has been
in an accident.

89
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:45,340
What?

90
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:46,480
(Emergency Medical Center)

91
00:06:51,150 --> 00:06:52,150
Oh no.

92
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,090
Excuse me.

93
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,990
Where can I find Cha Seong Woo?

94
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:00,490
Please head that way.

95
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:19,940
Ma'am, you shouldn't see him
like this. Allow us to...

96
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:52,740
Honey.

97
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:54,750
Seong Woo.

98
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:57,050
I'm here.

99
00:07:57,950 --> 00:07:59,480
Wake up, will you?

100
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:01,390
Honey.

101
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:05,020
- What do I do?
- Ma'am.

102
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:09,230
- Honey, wake up.
- Please calm down, ma'am.

103
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:11,460
- Honey, oh no!
- Ma'am, please calm down.

104
00:08:11,730 --> 00:08:14,000
- Seong Woo, wake up. I'm here.
- Ma'am.

105
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:15,930
Honey!

106
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,340
- Ma'am.
- Honey, no!

107
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,970
- Please calm down.
- Honey!

108
00:08:23,210 --> 00:08:24,410
Honey!

109
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:28,050
No, this can't be!

110
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:32,580
Honey, no...

111
00:08:58,780 --> 00:08:59,780
Honey...

112
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,650
Honey.

113
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,320
Honey...

114
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:07,820
I'm sorry.

115
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,020
Seok Jin.

116
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:15,890
What are we going to do?

117
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:21,730
(Cheongma)

118
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:26,100
Exactly how much
did they inflate the price?

119
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:29,170
Paintings that normally go
for 2,000 to 5,000 dollars...

120
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:32,480
seem to have sold for 200,000
to 300,000 dollars each.

121
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,580
Hold on.

122
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:36,310
Isn't that at least 50 or 60 times
the original price?

123
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:38,580
There appear to be
off-the-books buyers...

124
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,350
who aren't on the VIP list.

125
00:09:41,050 --> 00:09:44,090
It's likely that they're speculators
tied to the development site.

126
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:48,830
At this point,
Chairman Kim doesn't just stink.

127
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:50,560
He's a walking landfill.

128
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:53,660
Just secure the evidence for now.

129
00:09:54,070 --> 00:09:55,930
If we act rashly right now,

130
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,440
they will just cut their losses
and run.

131
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:00,070
Sure, I'll stand by for now.

132
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:04,780
I suppose it's time
for me to make a move.

133
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:10,580
These are tender tea leaves
that endured the cold winter wind,

134
00:10:10,650 --> 00:10:13,250
so the flavor
is very clear and delicate.

135
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:17,190
Shall we savor it slowly?

136
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,440
Is this your first time
at the tea house?

137
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:43,150
I used to just enjoy tea
alone at home,

138
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:46,050
but I heard about this gathering,
so I gathered the courage to come.

139
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,920
I still have a long way to go
and so much to learn.

140
00:10:48,990 --> 00:10:51,660
Gosh, not at all. Far from it.

141
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,160
From the way you pour the tea
and your breathing,

142
00:10:55,490 --> 00:10:57,800
I can feel
a different level of class.

143
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:00,160
It's a delightful sight.

144
00:11:01,070 --> 00:11:02,470
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

145
00:11:05,570 --> 00:11:07,340
Four, nine, two, one.

146
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,710
Is the owner of 4921 here?

147
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,210
Yes, what is this about?

148
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:15,250
You call that decent parking?

149
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:17,750
- Right, sorry about that.
- Move it already!

150
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,520
Right, I'm coming.
I'll move it right now.

151
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:20,920
Let's go.

152
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:39,540
My phone.

153
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,930
You sure stuffed yourself
with a lot, didn't you?

154
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:13,570
No wonder your stomach is bursting.

155
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,750
Ma'am.

156
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:31,090
Have you seen my phone?

157
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,960
No, I didn't see any phone.

158
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:36,190
Then where did I leave it?

159
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:38,330
Did you lose your phone, sir?

160
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,760
Gosh, this is bad.

161
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,030
I can't do without my phone.

162
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:43,800
Unbelievable.

163
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:59,080
Director Joo's secretary's office
told me to come help you out.

164
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,550
You know who I mean.

165
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:03,550
The tall and handsome secretary
who was recently hired.

166
00:13:09,390 --> 00:13:10,460
Excuse me.

167
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:15,700
Thank you for last time.

168
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,370
For what?

169
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:21,840
You asked the guard
outside the storage room...

170
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:23,210
to give me a hand.

171
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:26,280
Oh, that?

172
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:29,010
I wanted to help you myself,

173
00:13:29,310 --> 00:13:30,850
but I thought it might
make you feel uncomfortable,

174
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:32,680
so I asked the guard for a favor.

175
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:36,090
Everything went smoothly
because of your help.

176
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:37,150
Thank you.

177
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:39,420
Are you really thankful?

178
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:41,290
What?

179
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,230
If you're truly thankful,

180
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:48,130
how about having a meal together?

181
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:50,470
You see,

182
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,300
I'm still settling in,

183
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:54,910
so it's a bit awkward to eat alone.

184
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:57,110
I see.

185
00:13:57,710 --> 00:13:59,710
Eating alone in the cafeteria
feels kind of awkward.

186
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:02,080
You've been here longer,

187
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:04,010
so I'd love to join you...

188
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,650
if you don't mind.

189
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:09,850
Sure thing.

190
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,690
Since lunch hour is almost over,

191
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,260
it's gotten pretty quiet in here.

192
00:14:16,590 --> 00:14:18,200
Right, I suppose it is.

193
00:14:19,130 --> 00:14:21,800
Can I call you my senior?

194
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,100
Of course.

195
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:29,240
I heard you assist Director Joo.

196
00:14:30,810 --> 00:14:31,810
That's right.

197
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:34,110
Personally, I've always...

198
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:36,310
sincerely respected Ms. Joo.

199
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,680
You respect her?

200
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:40,150
When I was young,

201
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:43,150
I grew up in an orphanage.

202
00:14:45,490 --> 00:14:47,420
Thanks to the tuition
Ms. Joo sponsored,

203
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:49,960
I was able to safely graduate
from college.

204
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,500
I see.

205
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:55,030
Ms. Joo sponsored an orphanage?

206
00:14:55,370 --> 00:14:56,370
Yes.

207
00:14:57,170 --> 00:14:59,100
If it were not for her,

208
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,640
I likely would've
lost my way entirely by now.

209
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:07,540
Because of my background,

210
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:09,750
I was looked down upon
a lot everywhere.

211
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:13,380
So I wandered off the right path
quite a bit.

212
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:19,460
Back then,

213
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:23,460
it felt like the entire world
was pushing me away.

214
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:30,970
That must've been very hard for you.

215
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,110
My situation isn't entirely
the same,

216
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:39,880
but that feeling of being abandoned
by the whole world?

217
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:46,380
I can relate to that to some extent.

218
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,560
You know what's funny?

219
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:56,190
I feel like I open up
so easily around you.

220
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:02,430
I don't normally talk about myself
this easily around others.

221
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:06,870
Sometimes a casual relationship
is just easier.

222
00:16:09,810 --> 00:16:11,340
Who knows? It could grow deeper.

223
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:15,850
As colleagues at work,

224
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:19,880
we can at least discuss
our worries like this, right?

225
00:16:22,050 --> 00:16:23,620
Yes, of course.

226
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:43,410
I told you we should just buy some.

227
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,080
Does money grow on trees?

228
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,950
Mr. Park gave us
a ton of young radishes...

229
00:16:48,010 --> 00:16:49,810
he grew in his own garden.

230
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:51,620
All of this was free.

231
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:54,550
We could've just sold
those radishes for cash.

232
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:56,290
They're going to get thrown away
anyway.

233
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:58,060
You keep quiet.

234
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:01,020
You rejected all the women
that I set you up with.

235
00:17:01,930 --> 00:17:05,860
No one's going to offer
to set you up anymore.

236
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:08,030
Why did you even bother?

237
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:10,670
I need to figure myself out first
before I can date anyone.

238
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:13,340
Besides, now isn't the time
for me to be dating.

239
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,570
Shut it and give this a taste.

240
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:18,740
How is it?

241
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:23,650
Swallowing that
won't exactly kill you, son.

242
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:28,890
Grandma, taste it yourself.

243
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:30,590
You really need
to try this yourself.

244
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:31,660
What?

245
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:37,900
Hold on.
Are you sure this isn't spoiled?

246
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,770
I can't even understand
what you're saying.

247
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:42,830
Hold on a second.

248
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:45,700
I'll bring a real master chef over.

249
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,070
- What?
- What?

250
00:17:47,070 --> 00:17:48,840
Hey, where are you going
at this hour?

251
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:54,910
Then, I'll give it a try.

252
00:18:02,650 --> 00:18:05,520
Mom, is this food waste?

253
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,930
What? Food waste?

254
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,100
Seriously, ma'am?

255
00:18:25,010 --> 00:18:26,740
Here, please try some.

256
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:29,680
Wow, just the color alone...

257
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:36,350
That's what I'm talking about.

258
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:38,360
It just makes you want
a bowl of rice.

259
00:18:39,090 --> 00:18:40,660
Wait, let me get some rice.

260
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,860
Isn't my mom a great cook?

261
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,030
Teun Teun,

262
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:46,500
growing up with a mom
who's a great cook..

263
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,000
is a real blessing.

264
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:49,470
Take me, for example.

265
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,240
Man, I'm really jealous of you,
Teun Teun.

266
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,940
Jealous, my foot.

267
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:56,610
Then why don't you try some?

268
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:09,220
You're no master chef,
but you're still a pretty good cook.

269
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,720
Mi Rae, have you considered...

270
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,560
opening a boarding house?

271
00:19:15,390 --> 00:19:16,960
A boarding house sounds good.

272
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:20,800
Eun Guk, give me some rice.
I'd like some.

273
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,610
Chairman Kim, ma'am, you're here.

274
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:30,870
Ms. Kim.

275
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:32,710
- Ma'am, please have a seat.
- Thank you.

276
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:36,410
Thank you for coming all the way
out here. Please have a seat.

277
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,720
By the way, how did you know
to make a reservation here?

278
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:44,490
When the late chairman was alive,
I used to bring him here often.

279
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,930
I really wanted to bring you...

280
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:50,790
and your wife back here, sir.

281
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:52,160
I see.

282
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:57,300
Her late father
was very down-to-earth.

283
00:19:58,770 --> 00:20:00,870
Rather than fancy and neat places,

284
00:20:00,870 --> 00:20:04,580
he liked simple, warm places
like this.

285
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:07,480
Yes, that's right.

286
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:13,220
However, CEO Kang seems to have...

287
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:17,020
the exact opposite personality
of the late chairman.

288
00:20:18,790 --> 00:20:19,960
Is that so?

289
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:21,220
A person destined
for great things...

290
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,760
needs to know
how to quietly read the room.

291
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:26,130
But CEO Kang...

292
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,830
is a bit hasty.

293
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:32,140
I warn him from time to time,

294
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,200
but he's naturally so impatient...

295
00:20:34,770 --> 00:20:36,770
that my words
just don't get through to him.

296
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:39,680
It's only because it's me
that I can understand CEO Kang.

297
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:44,350
At the last gathering,
I was so embarrassed.

298
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:46,620
I am truly sorry, sir.

299
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:49,850
I deeply apologize once again.

300
00:20:49,850 --> 00:20:51,050
Please don't.

301
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:55,560
I didn't mention it
to get an apology from you.

302
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:56,790
Goodness.

303
00:20:56,990 --> 00:21:00,260
Anyway, for your sake,

304
00:21:00,330 --> 00:21:03,130
I'll make sure to handle
Cheongma's distribution carefully.

305
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:05,340
Don't worry too much. All right?

306
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,470
I leave it in
your capable hands, sir.

307
00:21:11,210 --> 00:21:12,210
Right.

308
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:21,950
I met Chairman Kim today.

309
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:25,960
Really? What did he say?

310
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:28,730
What do you think?

311
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:30,130
He said that for my sake,

312
00:21:30,730 --> 00:21:33,660
he'll help out
Cheongma's distribution.

313
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:36,370
Well, that's a given.

314
00:21:38,570 --> 00:21:40,870
What do you mean it's a given?

315
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:44,340
Do you know how sincerely
I apologized to him today?

316
00:21:44,340 --> 00:21:47,840
You're always so polite
when it comes to Chairman Kim.

317
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:49,780
Do you think I'm doing this for fun?

318
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:53,250
I'm just trying to fix your mess.

319
00:21:53,950 --> 00:21:55,750
Why are you being so twisted?

320
00:21:56,050 --> 00:21:59,390
I went and apologized on your behalf
for the mess you made.

321
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:01,960
Shouldn't you be thanking me?

322
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:05,030
You know,

323
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:08,030
time will tell
who you should truly...

324
00:22:08,530 --> 00:22:10,030
be thankful to.

325
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:13,670
What's his problem?

326
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:23,280
Chairman Kim sold
his wife's paintings...

327
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:25,280
for a hugely inflated price?

328
00:22:25,750 --> 00:22:27,950
The lands Chairman Kim
recently purchased...

329
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:31,590
seem to have been secured in advance
as locations for the new outlets.

330
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:35,230
And this is proof...

331
00:22:35,390 --> 00:22:37,460
that Chairman Kim's acquaintances
bought the land?

332
00:22:38,130 --> 00:22:39,130
Yes.

333
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:41,200
Since Chairman Kim couldn't
buy them directly,

334
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,970
his acquaintances
bought them instead...

335
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:45,040
and apparently split the profits.

336
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:48,470
It seems he's still looking into
the clan land in Gisan.

337
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:52,740
He acted like he was so clean,

338
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:55,050
but talk about having skeletons
in his closet.

339
00:22:56,050 --> 00:22:58,650
The more we dig,
the bigger the skeletons get.

340
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:01,820
From the looks of it, an even
bigger deal will take place...

341
00:23:01,890 --> 00:23:03,520
at the upcoming gallery event.

342
00:23:04,790 --> 00:23:06,520
Rather than going
for his throat right now,

343
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:07,820
it'd be more effective...

344
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:11,160
to draw our sword
when the time is right.

345
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:14,400
Right.

346
00:23:15,170 --> 00:23:16,730
Let's wait for the right time.

347
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,610
Yes, this is Joo Mi Ran.

348
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:31,820
Ae Sook, is that you? It's me.

349
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,750
Why do you keep
calling yourself Mi Ran...

350
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:37,620
instead of your pretty name,
Ae Sook?

351
00:23:39,890 --> 00:23:41,530
You have the wrong number.

352
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,430
Wrong number?

353
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:46,060
Do you think I'd forget
my Ae Sook's voice?

354
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:50,170
I bet you miss me too.

355
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,270
Just hang tight.

356
00:23:52,670 --> 00:23:55,170
I'll find you very soon.

357
00:24:02,510 --> 00:24:04,610
Go find An Guk Cheol right now.

358
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,220
Right. I've already
tracked his movements...

359
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,390
through the PI agency.

360
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,490
Don't make a move yet.

361
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:12,520
Approach him pretending to help,

362
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:14,830
and have him dancing
in the palm of your hand.

363
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:18,630
If you corner him out of nowhere,
there's no telling what he'll do.

364
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:21,330
Sure, I'll make my move right now.

365
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:24,600
Jun Hwan.

366
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:28,570
Yes, Ms. Joo.

367
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:32,080
I believe it's part of the process.

368
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,150
While trying to clean up my life,

369
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:37,910
I just happened
to get a little muddy,

370
00:24:39,450 --> 00:24:43,190
and I'm currently
wiping away the dirt.

371
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:44,650
That's my take on it.

372
00:24:46,390 --> 00:24:47,390
Of course.

373
00:24:48,230 --> 00:24:49,530
Whatever dirt you've got on you,

374
00:24:50,890 --> 00:24:52,500
I'll clean it right off.

375
00:25:03,110 --> 00:25:05,610
Director Joo hired a new secretary?

376
00:25:06,510 --> 00:25:09,250
Yes, it seems she hired
a new executive secretary,

377
00:25:09,310 --> 00:25:10,610
and a pretty young one at that.

378
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:13,080
Have you met him?

379
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:15,520
I bumped into him in the hallway.

380
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:17,820
I was moving
some defective samples at the time,

381
00:25:18,460 --> 00:25:19,760
and he helped me out.

382
00:25:20,390 --> 00:25:21,390
Is that so?

383
00:25:22,490 --> 00:25:25,960
Well, Ms. Joo probably needed
someone young to work with,

384
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:27,060
someone quicker on their feet.

385
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:32,870
But it seemed like his background
was quite similar to mine.

386
00:25:34,770 --> 00:25:35,840
In what way?

387
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:38,910
He grew up facing hardships
in an orphanage.

388
00:25:40,510 --> 00:25:42,450
I heard he even finished
his college studies...

389
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:44,920
with the scholarship
Ms. Joo sponsored.

390
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:47,580
That's why he trusts her
and is all the more loyal to her.

391
00:25:47,950 --> 00:25:49,650
His loyalty will be unwavering.

392
00:25:49,890 --> 00:25:52,120
He even called me his senior.

393
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,720
Having someone call me senior...

394
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:58,260
made me feel a heavy sense
of responsibility.

395
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:00,530
Of course.

396
00:26:00,530 --> 00:26:02,700
You can't stay the youngest one here
forever, Eun Seol.

397
00:26:02,870 --> 00:26:04,900
Exactly. It's fascinating.

398
00:26:12,310 --> 00:26:13,310
Still,

399
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:16,950
no matter how similar
your backgrounds are,

400
00:26:18,050 --> 00:26:20,150
don't trust them too much.

401
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:23,150
That's just
how workplace life works.

402
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,660
Right when you start believing
someone is on your side,

403
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:29,330
that is exactly
when they stab you in the back.

404
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:34,030
Things always happen
when you let your guard down.

405
00:26:36,100 --> 00:26:37,170
That's true.

406
00:26:37,630 --> 00:26:39,040
The closer they are,

407
00:26:39,470 --> 00:26:40,900
the more cautious you need to be.

408
00:26:43,670 --> 00:26:46,710
Then I should be the most careful
around you, Attorney Seo.

409
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:48,950
Me?

410
00:26:48,950 --> 00:26:51,110
You just said
I need to be most careful...

411
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:52,320
around those closest to me.

412
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:55,250
The person closest to me is you,

413
00:26:55,490 --> 00:26:57,320
so I should be the most careful
around you.

414
00:26:57,820 --> 00:27:00,290
Well, that's true, but...

415
00:27:00,420 --> 00:27:02,660
Come on, I should be an exception.

416
00:27:02,730 --> 00:27:03,730
That hurts a little.

417
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:06,500
- I'm only joking.
- Whatever.

418
00:27:06,860 --> 00:27:07,960
Buy me lunch, then.

419
00:27:11,100 --> 00:27:13,640
When will you be done?
We'll be late at this rate.

420
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:15,340
Let me finish this up.

421
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,310
It's already been 30 minutes.

422
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,940
I know. I'm almost done.

423
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:22,550
Done.

424
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:28,550
My parents rarely treat us,

425
00:27:28,750 --> 00:27:30,590
so couldn't you
wrap up work early today?

426
00:27:31,350 --> 00:27:33,160
I'm sorry. Let's get going. Come on.

427
00:27:33,620 --> 00:27:34,720
Let's hurry.

428
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:41,770
Seriously?

429
00:27:41,930 --> 00:27:43,970
Are Mom and Dad
still stuck in their meeting?

430
00:27:44,330 --> 00:27:46,740
The shareholders' meeting
must be running late.

431
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:49,770
Seriously,
why can nobody be on time?

432
00:27:51,010 --> 00:27:52,480
Where are your manners?

433
00:27:53,710 --> 00:27:54,940
And you have such great manners?

434
00:27:55,380 --> 00:27:57,750
Of course I do. I'm always on time.

435
00:27:58,450 --> 00:27:59,650
Stop pretending to be busy.

436
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:02,090
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

437
00:28:08,120 --> 00:28:09,290
Seok Jin, what do you have there?

438
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:10,930
What? It's nothing.

439
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:15,000
Gosh, we're sorry.

440
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:16,830
Did you wait long?

441
00:28:17,270 --> 00:28:19,640
What took you so long?
We might lose our dinner reservation.

442
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,700
I pushed it back.

443
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:23,710
- Let's go.
- Sure.

444
00:28:24,170 --> 00:28:25,240
Come on.

445
00:28:25,780 --> 00:28:27,980
Oh my, is someone pouting?

446
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:39,990
How are the store sales lately?

447
00:28:44,760 --> 00:28:47,900
They're increasing by
about 10 to 20 percent every week.

448
00:28:49,330 --> 00:28:52,840
It might just be the opening effect,
so don't let your guard down.

449
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:55,510
There are probably plenty
of people around you...

450
00:28:55,570 --> 00:28:58,410
who are hoping that
your initial momentum will die down.

451
00:28:59,540 --> 00:29:02,180
Of course.
I won't let my guard down.

452
00:29:03,150 --> 00:29:06,620
Dad, can we not talk shop
over dinner?

453
00:29:07,180 --> 00:29:10,650
She's right.
Let's just relax during the meal.

454
00:29:11,420 --> 00:29:13,690
Our future son-in-law
is going to get indigestion.

455
00:29:15,230 --> 00:29:16,660
To me, Chief Cha is...

456
00:29:17,230 --> 00:29:19,830
the general manager
of Cheongma's new brand.

457
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:23,830
Being my future son-in-law
is something to wait and see about.

458
00:29:24,470 --> 00:29:25,600
There you go again.

459
00:29:26,040 --> 00:29:28,470
It's so obvious when you try
to test him, you know.

460
00:29:30,340 --> 00:29:32,280
Who says I'm testing him?

461
00:29:40,150 --> 00:29:42,050
By the way,

462
00:29:42,820 --> 00:29:45,290
I noticed there was a lighter
on your desk, sir.

463
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:47,020
Oh, that?

464
00:29:47,190 --> 00:29:50,130
That lighter is like
my dad's comfort toy.

465
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:55,270
He doesn't even smoke,
but he cherishes it.

466
00:29:56,170 --> 00:29:58,870
If you think about it,
it's kind of cute.

467
00:29:59,470 --> 00:30:01,300
Oh, come on. Cute, really?

468
00:30:02,140 --> 00:30:03,870
It's an old habit I can't shake.

469
00:30:04,110 --> 00:30:06,210
That model must have been popular
back in the day.

470
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:11,010
Actually, a few days ago,

471
00:30:11,250 --> 00:30:13,580
I saw an identical one at my house.

472
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:16,420
An identical one?

473
00:30:16,890 --> 00:30:19,360
Yes, it was definitely
the same model.

474
00:30:21,060 --> 00:30:23,060
It's a vintage lighter,
so I guess that makes sense.

475
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:29,100
It must have been a model
that everyone wanted back then.

476
00:31:23,950 --> 00:31:27,190
(A Trap Called Desire)

477
00:31:27,990 --> 00:31:30,560
You know Chairman Min's son,
Min Jae Seong, right?

478
00:31:30,630 --> 00:31:32,300
How about him as a match
for our Hae Ra?

479
00:31:32,360 --> 00:31:33,700
As a match for Hae Ra?

480
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:37,200
I will dedicate my body and soul
to serve you, Eun Seol.

481
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:39,170
You've been flirting less lately.

482
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:41,940
But who knows how liquid courage
will make you flirt?

483
00:31:42,210 --> 00:31:43,910
I'm just scared of everything.

484
00:31:43,910 --> 00:31:46,110
Can the retrial even be held?

485
00:31:46,180 --> 00:31:49,110
Was Manager Na really the killer?

486
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:51,050
Will you be okay on your own?

487
00:31:51,050 --> 00:31:52,550
Director Joo can accompany me.

488
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:55,350
I'll prepare the gift
for Chairman Kim.

489
00:31:55,350 --> 00:31:57,890
I'll handle An Guk Cheol on my end.

490
00:31:57,890 --> 00:32:00,960
This is what you call
a perfect crime.

491
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:03,530
Flawless and perfect.

492
00:32:04,230 --> 00:32:06,200
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
